 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The error-handling property below remains outside the usage-accounting change in #93.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Turn usage — #93
+
+The chosen contract keeps one usage argument and sums provider calls. A separate per-round breakdown is rejected for this change because billing and budgets need the turn total and the wider surface is unnecessary. The hook signature must name the aggregate unambiguously (for example, `totalUsage?: TurnUsageMetadata` with the same numeric fields); the implementation must include a MINOR version bump and a changelog entry explaining that tool-heavy turns now record larger totals. The existing `receives collected response text and usage` test stays unedited to preserve the no-tool contract.
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once after the turn and receives the sum of `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` from every provider call, including both tool rounds and the final answer ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call after two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L61)).
+- Missing usage in any round is omitted from the sum without losing other rounds; a turn with no reported usage still receives `undefined` ([validated by: sums reported rounds across missing usage and preserves an entirely unreported turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
